      "result": {
        "reply_text": "You can approach the National Consumer Helpline (NCH) online at https://consumerhelpline.gov.in/ or by calling the toll-free numbers 1915 or 1800-11-4000 to lodge a grievance against the company for the defective product.\n\nA product liability action may be brought against a product manufacturer, service provider, or product seller for any harm caused by a defective product.\n\nA product manufacturer is liable in a product liability action if the product contains a manufacturing defect, design defect, deviation from manufacturing specifications, or does not conform to the express warranty.\n\nWhere the District Commission is satisfied that the goods suffer from defects, it may order the opposite party to replace the goods or return the price paid along with such interest as may be decided, and pay compensation.\n\nKeep your purchase bill and any photos or records of the defective charger ready.\n\nDid you contact the company for a refund yet?\n\nIs the charger still under warranty?\n\nSource: Department of Consumer Affairs - National Consumer Helpline (NCH), H NCH\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 84\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 39\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
